So, it seems like the summary, at least for the language stuff, should
actually be "Come up with a rather comprehensive list of fu'ivla, try to ge=
t
people to use them."  And then, maybe, at some point in the future if no on=
e
uses the gismu anymore, it might be time to revisit the issue of whether or
not to chuck them, but for now, there they stay.

I am happy to finish making up a list of terms from the list I was working
from, keeping in mind people's comments (especially given that, as .xorxes.
noted, there really isn't any reason to have them all be of the same
structure--I wonder about a couple of seven-letter fu'ivla would be better
for these).  I could then post it somewhere on the wiki for folks to take a
look at, make comments, changes, etc.  I guess my previous hesitation was
not so much about whether or not people would use this, but about whether o=
r
not people would be willing to look at the list and make some notes/changes
about things they don't like (a la Pierre's comment).  Based on the
responses here, it seems like there are at least a handful of people willin=
g
to do this, so I will try to cook up a list later this week and put it up
somewhere.

I will try to keep some notes on the list about various things (namely,
terms that don't come from the autonym).  I think we (well, I) need to thin=
k
about the autonym issue somewhat more--as with Finland, and with Chechen,
one could argue that the fact that the autonym is simply not used outside
the community of speakers, making the Lojban based on the autonym actually
introduces MORE cultural bias than going with the more international form.
I'm not sure I believe that, but it is worth thinking about while doing
this.

So, anyway, yeah--people will look at the list if I make it?  And tell me
how I did it all wrong? ;)

Chris

